=== Page & landmarks

--- Semantic page :: a11y-page html5s
Full HTML5 page: lang, viewport without zoom lock, skip link, header/nav/main/footer landmarks and one h1.
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="${1:en}">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>${2:Page title}</title>
  <meta name="description" content="${3:Page description}">
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>
  <header class="site-header">
    <a href="/" class="site-logo">${4:Site name}</a>
    <nav aria-label="Primary">
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/" aria-current="page">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="${5:/about}">${6:About}</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </header>
  <main id="main">
    <h1>${7:Page heading}</h1>
    $0
  </main>
  <footer class="site-footer">
    <p><small>&copy; ${CURRENT_YEAR} ${4}</small></p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>

--- Skip link :: a11y-skip
First focusable element on the page; jumps keyboard users past repeated navigation (WCAG 2.4.1).
<a class="skip-link" href="#${1:main}">${2:Skip to main content}</a>

--- Site header :: a11y-header
Site header landmark with a home link and labelled primary navigation.
<header class="site-header">
  <a href="/" class="site-logo">${1:Site name}</a>
  <nav aria-label="${2:Primary}">
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/" aria-current="page">${3:Home}</a></li>
      <li><a href="${4:/about}">${5:About}</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>
</header>

--- Navigation :: a11y-nav
Labelled nav landmark; aria-current marks the current page.
<nav aria-label="${1:Primary}">
  <ul>
    <li><a href="${2:/}" aria-current="page">${3:Home}</a></li>
    <li><a href="${4:/about}">${5:About}</a></li>
    <li><a href="${6:/contact}">${7:Contact}</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>

--- Breadcrumb :: a11y-breadcrumb
Breadcrumb nav as an ordered list; the last item carries aria-current="page".
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol>
    <li><a href="/">${1:Home}</a></li>
    <li><a href="${2:/section}">${3:Section}</a></li>
    <li><a href="${4:/section/page}" aria-current="page">${5:Current page}</a></li>
  </ol>
</nav>

--- Main :: a11y-main
Main landmark with the page's single h1; id="main" is the skip link target.
<main id="main">
  <h1>${1:Page heading}</h1>
  $0
</main>

--- Section :: a11y-section
Section named by its heading, so it is exposed as a region landmark.
<section aria-labelledby="${1:section}-title">
  <h2 id="${1}-title">${2:Section heading}</h2>
  $0
</section>

--- Article :: a11y-article
Self-contained article with heading, machine-readable date and author link.
<article>
  <header>
    <h2>${1:Article title}</h2>
    <p><time datetime="${CURRENT_YEAR}-${CURRENT_MONTH}-${CURRENT_DATE}">${CURRENT_DATE} ${CURRENT_MONTH_NAME} ${CURRENT_YEAR}</time> by <a href="${2:/author}" rel="author">${3:Author name}</a></p>
  </header>
  <p>${4:Article content}</p>
</article>

--- Aside :: a11y-aside
Complementary landmark named by its heading.
<aside aria-labelledby="${1:related}-title">
  <h2 id="${1}-title">${2:Related content}</h2>
  $0
</aside>

--- Site footer :: a11y-footer
Footer landmark with a labelled footer nav and accessibility statement link.
<footer class="site-footer">
  <nav aria-label="Footer">
    <ul>
      <li><a href="${1:/privacy}">${2:Privacy policy}</a></li>
      <li><a href="${3:/accessibility}">${4:Accessibility statement}</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>
  <p><small>&copy; ${CURRENT_YEAR} ${5:Site name}</small></p>
</footer>

--- Search :: a11y-search
Native search landmark with a visible label and submit button.
<search>
  <form action="${1:/search}" method="get">
    <label for="${2:site-search}">${3:Search the site}</label>
    <input type="search" id="${2}" name="${4:q}">
    <button type="submit">${5:Search}</button>
  </form>
</search>

=== Content

--- Screen-reader-only text :: a11y-sr
Text read by screen readers but hidden visually. Needs the a11y-visually-hidden CSS.
<span class="visually-hidden">${1:Text for screen reader users}</span>

--- Image :: a11y-img
Informative image with alt text and dimensions to prevent layout shift.
<img src="${1:image.jpg}" alt="${2:Describe what the image shows}" width="${3:800}" height="${4:600}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">

--- Decorative image :: a11y-img-deco
Decorative image with empty alt so screen readers skip it.
<img src="${1:decoration.svg}" alt="" width="${2:24}" height="${3:24}">

--- Figure :: a11y-figure
Image with a visible caption.
<figure>
  <img src="${1:image.jpg}" alt="${2:Describe what the image shows}" width="${3:800}" height="${4:600}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
  <figcaption>${5:Caption}</figcaption>
</figure>

--- Quote :: a11y-quote
Blockquote with source and attribution in a figure.
<figure>
  <blockquote cite="${1:https://example.com/source}">
    <p>${2:Quoted text}</p>
  </blockquote>
  <figcaption>${3:Author name}, <cite>${4:Source title}</cite></figcaption>
</figure>

--- Data table :: a11y-table
Table with caption and scoped column and row headers.
<table>
  <caption>${1:Table caption}</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">${2:Item}</th>
      <th scope="col">${3:Value}</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">${4:Row heading}</th>
      <td>${5:Data}</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

--- Description list :: a11y-dl
Term and description pairs.
<dl>
  <dt>${1:Term}</dt>
  <dd>${2:Description}</dd>
</dl>

--- Details :: a11y-details
Native disclosure widget; keyboard and screen reader support built in, no JS.
<details>
  <summary>${1:Summary}</summary>
  <p>${2:More details}</p>
</details>

--- Time :: a11y-time
Date with a machine-readable datetime value (defaults to today).
<time datetime="${1:${CURRENT_YEAR}-${CURRENT_MONTH}-${CURRENT_DATE}}">${2:${CURRENT_DATE} ${CURRENT_MONTH_NAME} ${CURRENT_YEAR}}</time>

--- Abbreviation :: a11y-abbr
Abbreviation with its expansion.
<abbr title="${1:World Wide Web Consortium}">${2:W3C}</abbr>

--- Language change :: a11y-lang
Marks a phrase in another language so screen readers switch pronunciation (WCAG 3.1.2).
<span lang="${1:fr}">${2:Bonjour}</span>

--- Contact address :: a11y-address
Contact details for the page or article owner.
<address>
  <a href="mailto:${1:hello@example.com}">${1}</a><br>
  <a href="tel:${2:+910000000000}">${2}</a>
</address>

--- Card :: a11y-card
Card with one link on the heading, so screen readers hear the link once.
<article class="card">
  <h3 class="card-title"><a href="${1:/post}">${2:Card title}</a></h3>
  <p>${3:Short summary}</p>
</article>

--- New-tab link :: a11y-link-new-tab
Link that opens a new tab and says so to screen reader users.
<a href="${1:https://example.com}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">${2:Link text}<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>

--- Icon button :: a11y-icon-btn
Icon-only button with a hidden text label and a hidden icon.
<button type="button" class="icon-button">
  <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24"><use href="#${1:icon-close}"></use></svg>
  <span class="visually-hidden">${2:Close}</span>
</button>

--- Decorative SVG :: a11y-svg-deco
Inline SVG hidden from assistive tech.
<svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24">$0</svg>

--- Meaningful SVG :: a11y-svg
Inline SVG exposed as an image with an accessible name.
<svg role="img" aria-labelledby="${1:graphic}-title" viewBox="0 0 ${2:24} ${3:24}" width="${2}" height="${3}">
  <title id="${1}-title">${4:Describe the graphic}</title>
  $0
</svg>

=== Media

--- Video :: a11y-video
Video with captions track, fallback download link and transcript link.
<video controls preload="metadata" width="${1:1280}" height="${2:720}" poster="${3:poster.jpg}">
  <source src="${4:video.mp4}" type="video/mp4">
  <track kind="captions" src="${5:captions.en.vtt}" srclang="${6:en}" label="${7:English}" default>
  <p>Your browser can't play this video. <a href="${4}">Download the video</a>.</p>
</video>
<p><a href="${8:#transcript}">Read the transcript</a></p>

--- Audio :: a11y-audio
Audio player with a title and transcript link.
<figure>
  <figcaption>${1:Audio title}</figcaption>
  <audio controls preload="metadata" src="${2:audio.mp3}"></audio>
  <p><a href="${3:#transcript}">Read the transcript</a></p>
</figure>

--- Iframe :: a11y-iframe
Embedded frame with a descriptive title.
<iframe src="${1:https://example.com/embed}" title="${2:Describe the embedded content}" width="${3:560}" height="${4:315}" loading="lazy" allowfullscreen></iframe>

=== Forms

--- Form :: a11y-form
Form shell with instructions and an explicit submit button.
<form action="${1:/submit}" method="${2|post,get|}">
  <p>${3:All fields are required unless marked optional.}</p>
  $0
  <button type="submit">${4:Submit}</button>
</form>

--- Text input :: a11y-input
Labelled input with hint text and autocomplete for input purpose (WCAG 1.3.5).
<div class="field">
  <label for="${1:full-name}">${2:Full name}</label>
  <p id="${1}-hint" class="hint">${3:As it appears on your ID}</p>
  <input type="${4|text,tel,url,number,date|}" id="${1}" name="${1}" autocomplete="${5|name,given-name,family-name,tel,organization,street-address,postal-code,url,off|}" aria-describedby="${1}-hint">
</div>

--- Email input :: a11y-email
Required email field with autocomplete.
<div class="field">
  <label for="${1:email}">${2:Email address}</label>
  <input type="email" id="${1}" name="${1}" autocomplete="email" spellcheck="false" required>
</div>

--- Password input :: a11y-password
Password field with hint and correct autocomplete for password managers.
<div class="field">
  <label for="${1:password}">${2:Password}</label>
  <p id="${1}-hint" class="hint">${3:Use 12 or more characters.}</p>
  <input type="password" id="${1}" name="${1}" autocomplete="${4|current-password,new-password|}" aria-describedby="${1}-hint" required>
</div>

--- Textarea :: a11y-textarea
Labelled multi-line text field.
<div class="field">
  <label for="${1:message}">${2:Message}</label>
  <textarea id="${1}" name="${1}" rows="${3:5}"></textarea>
</div>

--- Select :: a11y-select
Labelled select with a placeholder option.
<div class="field">
  <label for="${1:topic}">${2:Topic}</label>
  <select id="${1}" name="${1}">
    <option value="">${3:Choose a topic}</option>
    <option value="${4:general}">${5:General question}</option>
  </select>
</div>

--- Checkbox :: a11y-checkbox
Single checkbox with its label after the control.
<div class="field">
  <input type="checkbox" id="${1:agree}" name="${1}" value="${2:yes}">
  <label for="${1}">${3:I agree to the terms}</label>
</div>

--- Checkbox group :: a11y-checkboxes
Related checkboxes grouped by fieldset and legend; name[] submits every checked value.
<fieldset>
  <legend>${1:Which topics interest you?}</legend>
  <div>
    <input type="checkbox" id="${2:topics}-1" name="${2}[]" value="${3:design}">
    <label for="${2}-1">${4:Design}</label>
  </div>
  <div>
    <input type="checkbox" id="${2}-2" name="${2}[]" value="${5:development}">
    <label for="${2}-2">${6:Development}</label>
  </div>
</fieldset>

--- Radio group :: a11y-radios
Radio buttons grouped by fieldset and legend.
<fieldset>
  <legend>${1:How should we contact you?}</legend>
  <div>
    <input type="radio" id="${2:contact}-1" name="${2}" value="${3:email}">
    <label for="${2}-1">${4:Email}</label>
  </div>
  <div>
    <input type="radio" id="${2}-2" name="${2}" value="${5:phone}">
    <label for="${2}-2">${6:Phone}</label>
  </div>
</fieldset>

--- Field with error :: a11y-input-error
Invalid field: aria-invalid plus an error message linked by aria-describedby (WCAG 3.3.1).
<div class="field field-error">
  <label for="${1:email}">${2:Email address}</label>
  <p id="${1}-error" class="error-message"><span class="visually-hidden">Error:</span> ${3:Enter an email address like name@example.com}</p>
  <input type="${4:email}" id="${1}" name="${1}" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="${1}-error">
</div>

--- Error summary :: a11y-error-summary
List of errors linking to each field. Move focus here after a failed submit.
<div class="error-summary" tabindex="-1">
  <h2>${1:There is a problem}</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="#${2:email}">${3:Enter an email address}</a></li>
  </ul>
</div>

--- Progress :: a11y-progress
Labelled progress bar with a text fallback.
<label for="${1:upload-progress}">${2:Upload progress}</label>
<progress id="${1}" max="100" value="${3:40}">${3}%</progress>

=== Widgets & live regions

--- Dialog :: a11y-dialog
Native modal dialog opened with commandfor (no JS); focus trap and Escape built in.
<button type="button" commandfor="${1:dialog}" command="show-modal">${2:Open dialog}</button>
<dialog id="${1}" aria-labelledby="${1}-title">
  <h2 id="${1}-title">${3:Dialog title}</h2>
  <p>${4:Dialog content}</p>
  <form method="dialog">
    <button type="submit">${5:Close}</button>
  </form>
</dialog>

--- Disclosure :: a11y-disclosure
Show/hide button with aria-expanded. Pair with a11y-disclosure-js.
<button type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="${1:more-info}">${2:Show more}</button>
<div id="${1}" hidden>
  <p>${3:Hidden content}</p>
</div>

--- Mobile menu toggle :: a11y-nav-toggle
Navigation with a menu button using aria-expanded. Pair with a11y-disclosure-js.
<nav aria-label="${1:Primary}">
  <button type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="${2:primary-menu}">${3:Menu}</button>
  <ul id="${2}" hidden>
    <li><a href="/" aria-current="page">Home</a></li>
    <li><a href="${4:/about}">${5:About}</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>

--- Accordion item :: a11y-accordion
Accordion section: heading wrapping an aria-expanded button. Pair with a11y-disclosure-js.
<div class="accordion">
  <h3>
    <button type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="${1:faq}-panel-1">${2:Question}</button>
  </h3>
  <div id="${1}-panel-1" hidden>
    <p>${3:Answer}</p>
  </div>
</div>

--- Tabs :: a11y-tabs
ARIA tabs with roving tabindex. Pair with a11y-tabs-js for arrow-key support.
<div class="tabs">
  <div role="tablist" aria-label="${1:Product details}">
    <button type="button" role="tab" id="${2:tab}-1" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="${2}-panel-1">${3:Overview}</button>
    <button type="button" role="tab" id="${2}-2" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="${2}-panel-2" tabindex="-1">${4:Specs}</button>
  </div>
  <div role="tabpanel" id="${2}-panel-1" aria-labelledby="${2}-1" tabindex="0">
    <p>${5:Overview content}</p>
  </div>
  <div role="tabpanel" id="${2}-panel-2" aria-labelledby="${2}-2" tabindex="0" hidden>
    <p>${6:Specs content}</p>
  </div>
</div>

--- Toggle button :: a11y-toggle
On/off button using aria-pressed. Pair with a11y-toggle-js.
<button type="button" aria-pressed="false">${1:Mute}</button>

--- Switch :: a11y-switch
On/off switch using role="switch". Pair with a11y-toggle-js.
<button type="button" role="switch" aria-checked="false">${1:Dark mode}</button>

--- Pagination :: a11y-pagination
Labelled pagination with the current page marked and context for screen readers.
<nav aria-label="${1:Pagination}">
  <ul>
    <li><a href="${2:?page=1}">Previous<span class="visually-hidden"> page</span></a></li>
    <li><a href="?page=1" aria-current="page"><span class="visually-hidden">Page </span>1</a></li>
    <li><a href="?page=2"><span class="visually-hidden">Page </span>2</a></li>
    <li><a href="${3:?page=2}">Next<span class="visually-hidden"> page</span></a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>

--- Status message :: a11y-status
Polite live region (WCAG 4.1.3). Keep it in the page on load, then inject text.
<div role="status">$0</div>

--- Alert :: a11y-alert
Assertive live region for urgent messages. Keep it in the page on load, then inject text.
<div role="alert">$0</div>
